# Shemá — a avaliação de saúde: submissão, histórico e as perguntas-guia (BE-07 · OBT-396)
#
# `shema_record.http` beside this one is the ficha; this is the one tab of it whose data is an
# aggregate of its own. Four things are worth running by hand before believing the rest:
#
#   1. an assessment is a NEW ROW, never an edit. File two and read the history: both are there,
#      with their own dates and their own authors.
#   2. a BACKDATED reading does not overwrite a newer one. File today's, then file one dated
#      three months ago: the history grows and the record's flat fields do not move.
#   3. READ ACCESS IS NARROWER THAN THE RECORD'S. A `resourceCircle` account opens the ficha and
#      is refused the assessment — 200 on one path, 403 on the other, same account.
#   4. A DROP TO CRITICAL notifies the region's coordination and OBT Lab. Read it at
#      `GET /api/notifications` as the recipient and look at what it says: the team, the day,
#      the state, and where to go. No dimension, no note, no prayer request, no place.
#
# There is no `If-Match` here and that is deliberate: appending is not replacing, so there is
# nothing to be stale against. The new version comes back in the `ETag` all the same, because
# the record's flat health fields did move.
#
# Before running: seed the app and its roles, then grant two accounts so that 3 and 4 are real.
#   uv run python scripts/seed_apps_roles.py
#   uv run python scripts/grant_app_role.py mentoria.local@test.com shema obtLab
#   uv run python scripts/grant_app_role.py coordenacao.local@test.com shema coordinator
#   uv run python scripts/grant_app_role.py recursos.local@test.com shema resourceCircle
#   # the region scope is this module's own table; set it through the service or by SQL:
#   #   INSERT INTO shema_user_regions (user_id, region_key) VALUES ('<id>', 'south-america');

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8000
@slug = guarani-mbya

### Log in as the mentor — the OBT Lab holder who files the reading
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "mentoria.local@test.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

###
@token = {{login.response.body.access_token}}

### The guiding questions — what the wizard asks, and what every past set asked
# Provenance and not a rendering source: the console renders from its own constant, and this is
# how an entry stamped `questionSetVersion: 1` stays readable after the console ships set 2.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/shema/health-questions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 1 — file a reading. Four dimensions, a note per dimension, the set it answered.
# `notes` is NOT sent: the server derives the running blob from `dimensionNotes`, in the
# dimensions' own order. The reply is the recomputed record, and its ETag is the new version.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/shema/projects/{{slug}}/health-assessments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
X-Shema-Local-Date: 2026-09-11

{
  "date": "2026-09-11",
  "assessor": "Marina Alves",
  "emotional": "boa",
  "relational": "atencao",
  "spiritual": "boa",
  "physical": "boa",
  "dimensionNotes": {
    "emotional": "Eles estão firmes.",
    "relational": "Dois tradutores discutiram na semana passada."
  },
  "questionSetVersion": 1
}

### The history — oldest first. The last entry is what the record's flat fields project.
# Each entry carries `overall` (the worst of its own four, computed here), `questionSetVersion`
# and `author`. The `overall` of the last one is the record's `derived.health`.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/shema/projects/{{slug}}/health-assessments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 2 — a backdated reading. It lands in the history and moves nothing on the record.
# Read the history after this: two entries, `2026-06-01` first. Then read the record: the flat
# fields still say what the 11/sep reading said, because the team has been read since.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/shema/projects/{{slug}}/health-assessments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "date": "2026-06-01",
  "assessor": "Marina Alves",
  "emotional": "critica",
  "relational": "critica",
  "spiritual": "atencao",
  "physical": "boa"
}

### 4 — the drop to critical. File this, then read the coordinator's notifications.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/shema/projects/{{slug}}/health-assessments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "date": "2026-09-12",
  "assessor": "Marina Alves",
  "emotional": "critica",
  "relational": "atencao",
  "spiritual": "boa",
  "physical": "boa",
  "dimensionNotes": {
    "emotional": "Uma família está em crise e a equipe parou."
  },
  "needsPastoralIntervention": "sim",
  "pastoralInterventionName": "Marina Alves",
  "pastoralInterventionWhen": "now"
}

### Filing the same critical reading again announces nothing — the second telling is noise.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/shema/projects/{{slug}}/health-assessments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "date": "2026-09-13",
  "emotional": "critica",
  "relational": "atencao",
  "spiritual": "boa",
  "physical": "boa"
}

### What the coordinator received. Log in as them first.
# @name coordLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "coordenacao.local@test.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

###
@coordToken = {{coordLogin.response.body.access_token}}

### The notice — read what it says, and what it does not.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/notifications
Authorization: Bearer {{coordToken}}

### 3 — the Resource Circle opens the ficha…
# @name rcLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "recursos.local@test.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

###
@rcToken = {{rcLogin.response.body.access_token}}

### …200 here — they hold a Shemá role and the project's region.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/shema/projects/{{slug}}
Authorization: Bearer {{rcToken}}

### …and 403 here. Who may read a reading of a team is one key narrower (FE-44 §5.8).
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/shema/projects/{{slug}}/health-assessments
Authorization: Bearer {{rcToken}}

### Refused: a submission that rates nothing. A date with no rating reports a team as heard.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/shema/projects/{{slug}}/health-assessments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "date": "2026-09-14",
  "notes": "conversamos bastante"
}

### Refused: a question set this server never published.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/shema/projects/{{slug}}/health-assessments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "date": "2026-09-14",
  "emotional": "boa",
  "questionSetVersion": 99
}

### Refused: writing the flat projection directly. `recordAssessment` is its only writer.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/shema/projects/{{slug}}/health-assessments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "date": "2026-09-14",
  "emotional": "boa",
  "healthAssessor": "alguém"
}
